The medieval Latin texts of the Passio minor Kiliani and Passio maior Kiliani
are in the public domain.

All original material in this repository — the translations, apparatus, textual
notes, witness and edition lists, editorial history, genealogical analysis,
catalogue entries and accompanying prose — is offered under the Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0).

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

You may share and adapt this material for any purpose, including commercially,
provided you give appropriate credit, link to the licence, and indicate whether
changes were made.

Attribution: Nicholas Shane Kouns, "Sancti Kiliani" (2026).

Two things this licence does not cover:

  - Images of manuscripts held by the repositories named in this archive
    (St Gallen, Vienna, Munich, Hannover, Dublin, Karlsruhe, the Vatican Library
    and others). No such images are included here. Rights must be secured from
    the holding institution.

  - Museum photographs of the Augsburg engravings catalogued in family/.
    Accession numbers are given so that each work can be located; the images
    themselves are not reproduced and remain with the holding institutions.
